<h2>Segment 341 &mdash; enjoyments as objects</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s341S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w1">cha</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w2">gnyis pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w3">gzhi</span> ni <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w4">longs spyod</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w5">yin</span> te, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w6">sems can</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w7">nang</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w8">reg bya</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w9">longs spyod pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p10">las</span> byung ba <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p12">dang</span> , de <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p5">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w13">bdag tu <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s341m14">bzung ba</span></span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w15">dbang</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p16">gis</span> byung ba&#x27;i phyir</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s341S">The non-virtues of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w2">second</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w1">division</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w5">have</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w4">enjoyments</span> as their <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w3">object</span>: they occur <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p10">through</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w9">enjoyment</span> in the form of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w8">physical sensations</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w7">within</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w6">living being</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p12">or</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p16">by</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w15">force</span> of one&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s341w13"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s341m14">taking</span> possession</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s341p5">of</span> certain enjoyments.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Codex PROVISIONAL ROOT reconciliation, mechanically assembled by the Tibetan-original author. ROOT selects narrow nang/within and flat dbang/force plus whole gis/by; adds second la/of. Both byung ba predicates share one English occur and are omitted; first la/in and de/certain enjoyments remain uncertain. Exact original rationale/provenance and all changes are recorded separately. Source origin 58b6799188c8cb95f9095fea7cdc6bbf4d653894 through336; actual acceptance baseline 1e309d1cba99844e45d2bfef6285333c6945deee through339. No source/hgm_gloss edit or semantic acceptance.</div>
